{"answeredBy":"Ahsan (via web)","answers":{"Q-1":"No role distinctions; all users can view and operate all product areas.","Q-2":"Apply the ratio to consumption estimates and projections; record actual wastage separately only when entered as a movement.","Q-3":"Require the operator to enter a separate activity quantity for each affected lot.","Q-4":"Use as-fed pounds for total feed consumed and FCR, converting entered inventory units to pounds as needed.","Q-5":"Report feed cost per pound of gain only; do not label it full ROI or profitability."},"asked":[{"category":"roles","difference":"D-8","id":"Q-1","impact":3,"impactReason":"Roles control who can write operational records and who can see potentially sensitive cost and performance information.","options":["No role distinctions; all users can view and operate all product areas.","Use a small built-in set of roles, such as administrator, operator, and viewer, with cost/performance access controlled by role.","Define configurable roles and per-action permissions, including record-level access to yards, lots, and pens."],"reason":"No roles or restricted audiences are required by the request, so a shared access model is the smallest implementation.","recommended":"No role distinctions; all users can view and operate all product areas.","score":9,"spans":["I-1","I-3","I-4","I-5","I-6","I-8","I-9","I-10"],"text":"Which user roles and access boundaries are required for operational records, cost/performance views, imports, and data entry?","topic":"roles","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","difference":"D-3","id":"Q-2","impact":3,"impactReason":"The choice changes stock balances and whether wastage is counted once or potentially twice.","options":["Apply the ratio to consumption estimates and projections; record actual wastage separately only when entered as a movement.","Treat the ratio as the actual wastage movement and decrement stock by it whenever feed is consumed.","Apply the ratio to estimates and projections, and also let users record actual wastage movements separately."],"reason":"This avoids inventing actual losses while supporting the requested configurable forecast adjustment.","recommended":"Apply the ratio to consumption estimates and projections; record actual wastage separately only when entered as a movement.","score":9,"spans":["I-3"],"text":"Should the wastage ratio represent only forecasted/estimated losses, or should actual wastage also be recorded as a separate stock movement?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-3","impact":3,"impactReason":"Attribution directly changes lot feed consumption, feed cost, FCR, and cost of gain.","options":["Require the operator to enter a separate activity quantity for each affected lot.","Allocate the pen's actual quantity and cost among its lots in proportion to animal count at the time of feeding.","Attribute the full pen activity to one selected lot; record separate activities for other lots."],"reason":"Explicit lot quantities avoid double-counting and do not assume that every lot received the same amount per animal.","recommended":"Require the operator to enter a separate activity quantity for each affected lot.","score":9,"spans":["I-5","I-7","I-8"],"text":"When one pen contains multiple lots, how should a feeding activity's actual quantity and cost be attributed to lot-level metrics?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-4","impact":3,"impactReason":"The basis changes reported feed consumption and the resulting FCR values.","options":["Use as-fed pounds for total feed consumed and FCR, converting entered inventory units to pounds as needed.","Convert feed to dry-matter pounds using each ingredient's dry-matter percentage before calculating FCR.","Show both as-fed and dry-matter FCR."],"reason":"The request defines total feed consumed in pounds and does not require a dry-matter-adjusted metric.","recommended":"Use as-fed pounds for total feed consumed and FCR, converting entered inventory units to pounds as needed.","score":9,"spans":["I-3","I-4","I-5","I-7","I-9"],"text":"Should feed-to-gain calculations use feed on an as-fed basis or adjust feed consumption to dry matter?","topic":"terminology","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-5","impact":3,"impactReason":"A full ROI calculation adds financial inputs and could materially change profitability claims.","options":["Report feed cost per pound of gain only; do not label it full ROI or profitability.","Calculate full lot ROI using purchase cost, feed cost, sale proceeds, and any other specified operating costs.","Show feed cost and procurement cost, but omit ROI until sale proceeds and other costs are available."],"reason":"Feed cost per gain is explicitly defined; full ROI needs sale proceeds and additional cost inputs not specified in the request.","recommended":"Report feed cost per pound of gain only; do not label it full ROI or profitability.","score":9,"spans":["I-1","I-7","I-8"],"text":"Does 'lot-level profitability/ROI' require more than the specified feed cost per unit of weight gain?","topic":"reporting","uncertainty":3}],"assumptions":[{"fromQuestion":"Q1","fromSpan":["I-1","I-10"],"id":"ASM-1","risk":"high","text":"How should procurement and receiving data connect to the primary procurement system for this build? → assumed: Use clearly labelled mock/source data only; no live connector is required."},{"fromQuestion":"Q2","fromSpan":["I-1"],"id":"ASM-2","risk":"high","text":"What should happen when an import contains duplicate source identifiers, an unmatched PO line or lot, or a lot-to-pen assignment exceeding capacity? → assumed: Report row-level problems, keep unmatched records out of downstream pen operations, reject over-capacity assignments, and prevent duplicate imports from double-counting records."},{"fromQuestion":"Q3","fromSpan":["I-2","I-7"],"id":"ASM-3","risk":"low","text":"Which gain-rate assumption should drive projected market dates when current lot performan